{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/707388-how-to-play-a-samsa","id":707388,"title":"How to play a Samsa","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-18T14:32:04-07:00","id":707388,"title":"How to play a Samsa","content":"Well, ever since I saw the Book of the Wyrm, the Samsa, Pentex' very own cockroaches, stuck to me. And, finally, I got a DM who will allow me to play one of those. So I'm currently trying my best at fleshing out a character and I could really use some input. The basic story of the character, still in need of elaboration, is this: <br /> <br /> Gregor has grown up on the streets, being an orphan since he can remember. Various orphanages tried their best to socialize him, but he always broke out and went out on the streets. He got through with a little bit of everything - selling drugs, breaking and entering, the few oddjobs people on the streets have for a small nimble guy who can think for himself but is smart enough usually not to do so. Being an opportunist through and through he wasn't above taking some more shady jobs as well, such as a &quot;Medication Study&quot; performed by a local company. By faking a few documents he got himself in as &quot;Gregor Schopenhauer&quot;, a fake identity he used to get around. He learned just what exactly that medication was supposed to cure and he made sure to fake the symptoms of that disease - after all he was going to sell the pills he got to some idiot junkie and take the studies money to boot. Sadly, however, this study was a mere pretense to get appropriate Test Subjects for a revival of &quot;Project Metamorphosis&quot; by Pentex' German Branch. And Gregor fit the bill perfectly. So perfectly in fact, he got knocked over the head the very next day and when he woke up from troubled dreams, he found himself transformed in his bed into a horrible vermin...<br /> <br /> The character is from Germany, Bochum to be precise, thus the re-iteration of the Metamorphosis Project. In terms of character he is a big conspiracy theorist with the usual derangement of the Samsa having multiplied his distrust in the authorities to a heavy degree. <br /> <br /> Questions that come to mind for me personally are those: How would a Samsa deal with Garou? Would he know they are &quot;different&quot; or just see them as potential enemies? What would Pentex do to reclaim their little bug-friend, assuming he managed to escape and they know about it? What are ways that Cockroach might try to contact him? <br /> Also, I'm all open for suggestions on how to re-write the character, either in terms of personality or biography.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8325-asmael","name":"Asmael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T15:05:40-07:00","id":707477,"title":"","content":"I guess the bigger question would be how would the Garou deal with you? I would imagine some Wyrm taint is involved and the intrinsic distrust in authorities will cause friction with the elders should a pack &quot;take him in&quot;. I would also wager that pentex would use their &quot;bug&quot; to find the careen, high ranking elders and kin folk, them plan accordingly. As for cockroach contacting you I would guess probably dreams maybe little &quot;emissaries&quot; but given his conspiracy prone mind it could ether cause a mental breakdown or a spiritual awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T16:47:59-07:00","id":707722,"title":"","content":"This is a very cool opportunity!<br /> <br /> But first: you are actually naming the thing Gregor? I mean, I know it is an alias but c'mon, bit on the nose, isn't it? Most of us don't name our werewolf PC's Lon Chaney. :P<br /> <br /> Samsa are all severely mentally ill. Those fractures in your psyche will be pretty important, and likely define whatever personality is left after poor Mr. Schopenhauer's traumatic first change. In addition to the natural paranoia of this particular mockery breed, what other derangements are you considering?<br /> I would also suggest a devising mild way to circumvent the paranoia in specific circumstances; it can really strain credibility when you eventually have to trust other players or NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T22:49:38-07:00","id":708189,"title":"","content":"A Samsa first will be insane, paranoia and perhaps a dash of either OCD or schizophrenia. OCD is almost always accompanied by severe anxiety and panic attacks. If you're going with OCD you and the ST need to work out Gregor's triggers. For example Gregor drinks coffee, it must be in a 16 ounce cup and he needs 4 packets of sugar, two creamers, and must stir it counter clockwise six times. His daily rituals if interrupted lead to severe anxiety and can ramp up to full blown panic attacks. Schizophrenia hearing voices and arguing with them out loud is another possibility.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T05:04:04-07:00","id":708515,"title":"","content":"Screws coffee, go strait sugar water ala men in black. <br /> <br /> I'm assuming Gregor is a reference based on previous responses, and I applaud literary references (if that's what that is).<br /> <br /> I think for garou cohesion, a glass walker in contact with cockroach spirits may lead to them finding Gregor, a paranoid wreck terrified of the voices (cockroach) he hears in the dark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T02:20:54-07:00","id":710212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics Of War</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/707388-how-to-play-a-samsa?p=708515#post708515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Screws coffee, go strait sugar water ala men in black. <br /> <br /> I'm assuming Gregor is a reference based on previous responses, and I applaud literary references (if that's what that is).<br /> <br /> I think for garou cohesion, a glass walker in contact with cockroach spirits may lead to them finding Gregor, a paranoid wreck terrified of the voices (cockroach) he hears in the dark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Samsa itself is a reference for it. It's from Kafkas book &quot;The Metamorphosis&quot; the protagonist is callers Gregor Samsa. Interesting book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5970-meldok","name":"Meldok","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"221"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T02:32:49-07:00","id":710222,"title":"","content":"While not a full derangement I think some sort of memory loss everytime he uses swarm would be cool. Makes me wanna watch mimic again","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T04:13:29-07:00","id":710349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/707388-how-to-play-a-samsa?p=710222#post710222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While not a full derangement I think some sort of memory loss everytime he uses swarm would be cool. Makes me wanna watch mimic again</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't that already a side effect that happens when they enter crawlings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T04:19:29-07:00","id":710354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/707388-how-to-play-a-samsa?p=710349#post710349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Isn't that already a side effect that happens when they enter crawlings?</div> </div> </div> </div>To the werespider's yes but only if the &quot;brain spiders&quot; get smashed. These samsa only have two forms, human and crinos sized cockroach. They can however &quot;swarm&quot; in this form creating about a dozen little cockroaches they control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T04:38:53-07:00","id":710369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/707388-how-to-play-a-samsa?p=710354#post710354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To the werespider's yes but only if the &quot;brain spiders&quot; get smashed. These samsa only have two forms, human and crinos sized cockroach. They can however &quot;swarm&quot; in this form creating about a dozen little cockroaches they control.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See the way I read that is that they can only swarm when they take a death blow and it doesn't matter if brain bugs get smashed, they always experience memory loss of several hours leading up to when they 'died'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-20T04:57:23-07:00","id":710375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/707388-how-to-play-a-samsa?p=710369#post710369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> See the way I read that is that they can only swarm when they take a death blow and it doesn't matter if brain bugs get smashed, they always experience memory loss of several hours leading up to when they 'died'.</div> </div> </div> </div>I read it as they explode into a crawlering esk form when they take a death blow, kinda like a death frenzy but with more fleeing.<br /> <br /> The swarming when in big bug mode is more of a hive sorta thing so maybe schizophrenia as his psyche gets pulled in a couple directions at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}